/ INTCODE UART loader.  Assembled high in the store (INTCODE_BASE=26000) so that what it loads can occupy 0..25999.
/ It reads commands from the console, white space between them ignored:
/   W aaaaaaaa dddddddd     store the word d (8 hex digits) at address a (8 hex digits)
/   G pppppppp              P := p and jump to word 402, where a program's start-up stub is (load and run it)
/ No library, no subroutines: the operate codes X26 (read a character) and X27 (write one) do the I/O, so overwriting the low store
/ (the program's globals at 1.., its stub at 402..) cannot disturb it.  The cells are 1 V, 2 N, 3 PH, 4 AD, 6 C, 7 D.
 L0 SL3
 L76 X27 L79 X27 L65 X27 L68 X27 L10 X27
10 X26 SL6
 LIL6 L87 X10 TL20
 LIL6 L71 X10 TL30
 JL10
20 L0 SL3 JL40
30 L2 SL3 JL40
40 L0 SL1 L8 SL2
41 X26 SL6
 LIL6 L15 X18 SL7
 LIL6 L64 X14 FL42
 LIL7 L9 X8 SL7
42 LIL1 L4 X16 LIL7 X19 SL1
 LIL2 L1 X9 SL2
 LIL2 TL41
 LIL3 FL50
 LIL3 L1 X10 TL60
 L402 LIL1 X32
50 LIL1 SL4 L1 SL3 JL40
60 LIL1 SIL4 JL10
1 D0
2 D0
3 D0
4 D0
6 D0
7 D0
